    "q-78208": {
      "dom_id": "step-q78208",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find the equation of the osculating plane (in parametric form) for a curve $r(t)$ at the point $P(0,1,0)$ where $t=1$, given that\n\n$$\nT(1)=\\frac{1}{5}(3\\,i+4\\,k),\\,N(1)=j.\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively.",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that the position vector of the point $P(0,1,0)$ is $r(1)=j.$\n\nThe osculating plane passes through the point that is at the tip of the vector $r(1).$ The vectors $T(1)$ and $N(1)$ are parallel to this plane. Therefore, the equation of the plane (in parametric form) can be written as\n\n$$\nR(s,u)=r(1)+s\\,T(1)+u\\,N(1),\\,s,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\n \n\nHence, the equation of the osculating plane at the point $(0,1,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s,u) & =r(1)+s\\,T(1)+u\\,N(1) \\\\  & =j+\\frac{s}{5}(3\\,i+4\\,k)+u(j) \\\\  & =\\frac{3s}{5}\\,i+(1+u)\\,j+\\frac{4s}{5}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
